From 579c39be3468214f5ed4aad6b1a0f49ff928e8d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReArc Overlay <overlay@rearc.invalid>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:47:50 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 wave 18g: route HTTP authentication through the
 host

Use a registry LoginHandler for Basic/Digest challenge requests and credential responses, preserving Chromium auth caching and password-manager bookkeeping. Cancel without a host callback; withdraw on handler/navigation teardown, callback replacement and tab/profile/engine close. Permit registry subresource challenges to reach the handler without a modal-dialog manager. ABI 1.38 / bridge 0.40.0 (http_auth); p93 and local Basic retry/Digest/cancel/replacement/pending-close fixture pass with no outside connections. TLS client certificate selection is deferred for a separate identity/private-key lifetime and isolated mutual-TLS harness.

Last rebased: 2026-11-04 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.74 (d331de35ca).

Co-Authored-By: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
